Title: THE SUMMIT NOTE
Author: Alex Rivera
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. NEPAL BASE CAMP - DAY

Prayer flags snap in thin air. CLIMBER JUNE OKAFOR, 35, checks crampons. Guide TENZIN adjusts her harness. A WAX-SEALED ENVELOPE bulges in June's chest pocket.
TENZIN
Summit window closes in thirty-six hours. Weather turns after.

EXT. ICE FALL - DAY

The team picks through blue ice. June pauses at a cairn — a tin box with a name: M. OKAFOR, 1987.
JUNE
My father turned back fifty meters below the ridge. Never told me why.

INT. TENT - NIGHT

June opens the leather pouch by headlamp — her father's handwriting. Coordinates, a sketch of a cave below the summit.
JUNE
He wasn't turning back from the mountain. He was turning toward something.

EXT. SUMMIT RIDGE - DAWN

Wind screams. June and Tenzin crest the ridge — not the true summit, but a fissure in the face, exactly where the sketch indicated.
TENZIN
We have twenty minutes. Then we descend or we die polite.

INT. ICE CAVE - DAY

Lantern glow on stacked survey crates — British expedition, 1985. June finds her father's journal, last entry unfinished.
JUNE
He found proof the peak was wrong by forty meters. They buried it to keep the record.

FADE OUT.


THE END
